{
  "_id": "ooMa1mHrp4H4excR",
  "name": "The Wayreth Bestiary: Illustrated",
  "pages": [
    {
      "_id": "fQ3OjnOf71P5Ea9t",
      "name": "The Plates",
      "type": "text",
      "title": {
        "show": true,
        "level": 1
      },
      "text": {
        "format": 1,
        "content": "<div class=\"wayreth-journal\">\n<p class=\"wy-lead\">Every creature in the bestiary, with its art, so you can show the table what they are looking at instead of describing it.</p>\n<p>81 creatures across 7 creature types, each plate running from the weakest to the strongest. Each entry carries the numbers worth knowing before you commit to an encounter &mdash; challenge rating, armour class, hit points, size and type. The full stat block lives on the Actor itself in <strong>Wayreth — Bestiary</strong>.</p>\n<table class=\"wy-table\"><thead><tr><th>Plate</th><th>Creatures</th><th>CR</th><th>When</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><strong>Aberration</strong></td><td>2</td><td>9&ndash;13</td><td>Arc IV, the Silvanesti expedition.</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Beast</strong></td><td>1</td><td>1&ndash;1</td><td>Arc I, the thirty-nine days.</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Dragon</strong></td><td>35</td><td>1&ndash;27</td><td>Draconians from Arc I. Wyrmlings and young from Arc II. Ancients are Arcs V and VI.</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Fiend</strong></td><td>7</td><td>4&ndash;18</td><td>Arc III in ones and twos. Arc VI in earnest.</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Humanoid</strong></td><td>26</td><td>0&ndash;21</td><td>Throughout.</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Plant</strong></td><td>2</td><td>6&ndash;7</td><td>Arc I at the forest edge; Arc IV in the dream.</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Undead</strong></td><td>8</td><td>4&ndash;22</td><td>Arc III onward; the Returned define Arc V.</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<h3>Showing These to Players</h3>\n<p>The plates are ordinary journal images, so right-clicking one and choosing to show it to players works as it does anywhere else. The art has a transparent background, which is why the tokens sit cleanly on a map rather than arriving in a box.</p>\n<p>Nothing here spoils anything by itself, but the <strong>Humanoid</strong> plate runs from a Dragonarmy recruit up through the Conclave to Raistlin, which makes it the cast list for the whole campaign. It is the one page worth keeping to yourself.</p>\n</div>"
      },
